    Bug 2035751 - Fix MimePartBufferReset() UAF. r=kaie,jtracey

    Failure to null the data->part_buffer pointer and resetting part_buffer_size can lead for
    the `if (!data->part_buffer && !data->file_buffer)` check in MimePartBufferWrite() to fail due to the dangling pointer,
    so no new buffer is allocated. If that buffer is then reallocated and written into we get UAF.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297265

diff --git a/mailnews/mime/src/mimepbuf.cpp b/mailnews/mime/src/mimepbuf.cpp
index ebf62737390..f4fbf81ded6 100644
--- a/mailnews/mime/src/mimepbuf.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/mime/src/mimepbuf.cpp
@@ -82,7 +82,9 @@ void MimePartBufferReset(MimePartBufferData* data) {
   if (!data) return;

   PR_FREEIF(data->part_buffer);
+  data->part_buffer = nullptr;
   data->part_buffer_fp = 0;
+  data->part_buffer_size = 0;

   if (data->input_file_stream) {
     data->input_file_stream->Close();
@@ -182,6 +184,7 @@ int MimePartBufferWrite(MimePartBufferData* data, const char* buf,
       }

       PR_FREEIF(data->part_buffer);
+      data->part_buffer = nullptr;
       data->part_buffer_fp = 0;
       data->part_buffer_size = 0;
     }
